From: any444v <162444641+any444v@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cad-pulse: apply the mic state to new sources

With UCM device-combination profiles every profile switch (call start,
speaker on/off) brings a new source, and the audio server restores the
mute state it saved for it. Hanging up while muted left the call source
muted for the next call while callaudiod reported the mic as on. Apply
the tracked mic state to a source when it appears.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
diff --git a/src/cad-pulse.c b/src/cad-pulse.c
index 7a203e6..d0c1502 100644
--- a/src/cad-pulse.c
+++ b/src/cad-pulse.c
@@ -206,6 +206,18 @@ static void init_source_info(pa_context *ctx, const pa_source_info *info, int eo
         else
             self->mic_state = CALL_AUDIO_MIC_ON;
         g_object_set(self->manager, "mic-state", self->mic_state, NULL);
+    } else if (!!info->mute != (self->mic_state == CALL_AUDIO_MIC_OFF)) {
+        /*
+         * A source that appears with a profile switch comes with the mute
+         * state the audio server restored for it, e.g. still muted from
+         * the end of the previous call. Apply the state we report.
+         */
+        g_debug("SOURCE: applying mic state %d", self->mic_state);
+        op = pa_context_set_source_mute_by_index(ctx, self->source_id,
+                                                 self->mic_state == CALL_AUDIO_MIC_OFF,
+                                                 NULL, NULL);
+        if (op)
+            pa_operation_unref(op);
     }
 
     target_port = get_available_source_port(info, NULL);
